 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# AI Music Usage Tutorial (Interactive)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook mirrors the scripts in `scripts/` and walks through the process step-by-step using pandas DataFrames.\n",
    "\n",
    "You'll learn how to:\n",
    "- Create folders and manage paths\n",
    "- Read CSVs into DataFrames\n",
    "- Group and aggregate data\n",
    "- Collect Google Trends monthly time series (no API key required)\n",
    "- Plot usage trends over time and save figures\n",
    "\n",
    "Prerequisites:\n",
    "- Run the cells below to install dependencies.\n",
    "- No API keys required here (YouTube is optional and skipped).\n",
    "\n",
    "Tip: A pandas DataFrame behaves like an in-memory spreadsheet: rows + named columns.\n",
    "We can filter, group, and aggregate it just like using pivot tables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required libraries (safe to run multiple times)\n",
    "%pip install -q pandas requests matplotlib huggingface_hub pytrends\n",
    "\n",
    "# If %pip is unsupported in your environment, run these in a terminal instead:\n",
    "#   pip install pandas requests matplotlib huggingface_hub pytrends"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1) Imports and folder setup\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use `pathlib.Path` for folders, and create `data/`, `data/sonics/`, and `figures/` if they don't exist.\n",
    "\n",
    "No DataFrames yet—just preparing the filesystem for later steps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import datetime\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download\n",
    "from pytrends.request import TrendReq\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define folders\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path(\"data\")\n",
    "SONICS_DIR = DATA_DIR / \"sonics\"\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR = Path(\"figures\")\n",
    "\n\",\n    "# Create them if needed\n",
    "DATA_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "SONICS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR, SONICS_DIR, FIGURES_DIR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Download SONICS metadata (fake_songs.csv, real_songs.csv)\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `huggingface_hub.snapshot_download` to fetch the dataset. We then read the CSV files into DataFrames using `pd.read_csv`.\n",
    "\n",
    "DataFrame basics you will see:\n",
    "- `pd.read_csv(path)` loads a CSV into a DataFrame.\n",
    "- `df.head()` shows the first few rows.\n",
    "- `len(df)` returns the number of rows.\n",
    "- `list(df.columns)` returns the column names."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download SONICS metadata (skip audio files)\n",
    "cache_dir = snapshot_download(\n",
    "    repo_id=\"awsaf49/sonics\",\n",
    "    repo_type=\"dataset\",\n",
    "    local_dir=str(SONICS_DIR),\n",
    "    ignore_patterns=[\"*.mp3\", \"*.wav\", \"*.flac\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Locate the CSV files\n",
    "fake_csv = None\n",
    "real_csv = None\n",
    "for root, _, files in os.walk(cache_dir):\n",
    "    for f in files:\n",
    "        if f == \"fake_songs.csv\":\n",
    "            fake_csv = Path(root) / f\n",
    "        elif f == \"real_songs.csv\":\n",
    "            real_csv = Path(root) / f\n",
    "\n",
    "df_fake = pd.read_csv(fake_csv) if fake_csv else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "df_real = pd.read_csv(real_csv) if real_csv else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"fake_songs.csv rows:\", len(df_fake))\n",
    "print(\"fake_songs.csv columns:\", list(df_fake.columns))\n",
    "display(df_fake.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"real_songs.csv rows:\", len(df_real))\n",
    "print(\"real_songs.csv columns:\", list(df_real.columns))\n",
    "display(df_real.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save a copy to our target paths for consistency\n",
    "(SONICS_DIR / \"fake_songs.csv\").write_text(df_fake.to_csv(index=False))\n",
    "(SONICS_DIR / \"real_songs.csv\").write_text(df_real.to_csv(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Aggregate SONICS\n",
    "\n",
    "We group and count by key fields. This is similar to a pivot table:\n",
    "- `df.groupby(\"col\").size()` counts rows per unique value in `col`.\n",
    "- `.reset_index(name=\"count\")` converts the Series back to a DataFrame with a named `count` column.\n",
    "\n",
    "Outputs:\n",
    "- `data/sonics/fake_counts_by_source.csv`\n",
    "- `data/sonics/fake_counts_by_label.csv` (if label column exists)\n",
    "- `data/sonics/real_counts_by_year.csv` (if year column exists)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Group by source (Suno/Udio) and count\n",
    "counts_by_source = df_fake.groupby(\"source\").size().reset_index(name=\"count\")\n",
    "display(counts_by_source.head())\n",
    "counts_by_source.to_csv(SONICS_DIR / \"fake_counts_by_source.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Group by label if present\n",
    "if \"label\" in df_fake.columns:\n",
    "    counts_by_label = df_fake.groupby(\"label\").size().reset_index(name=\"count\")\n",
    "    display(counts_by_label.head())\n",
    "    counts_by_label.to_csv(SONICS_DIR / \"fake_counts_by_label.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No 'label' column in fake_songs.csv; skipping label aggregate.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count real songs per year if present\n",
    "if \"year\" in df_real.columns:\n",
    "    counts_by_year = df_real.groupby(\"year\").size().reset_index(name=\"count\")\n",
    "    display(counts_by_year.head())\n",
    "    counts_by_year.to_csv(SONICS_DIR / \"real_counts_by_year.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No 'year' column in real_songs.csv; skipping year aggregate.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4) Google Trends monthly time series (no API key)\n",
    "\n",
    "Google Trends returns weekly data by default. We'll:\n",
    "- Request interest over time for keywords\n",
    "- Drop `isPartial` if present\n",
    "- Resample weekly -> monthly start (`MS`) using `.resample(\"MS\").mean()`\n",
    "- Save to `data/google_trends_ai_music.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: Google Trends values are normalized (0–100) and indicate relative interest."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "queries = [\"AI generated music\", \"AI music\", \"Suno\", \"Udio\", \"Boomy\"]\n",
    "start = datetime.date(2023, 1, 1)\n",
    "end = datetime.date.today().replace(day=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "pytrends = TrendReq(hl=\"en-US\", tz=360)\n",
    "timeframe = f\"{start.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} {end.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}\"\n",
    "pytrends.build_payload(kw_list=queries, timeframe=timeframe, geo=\"\")\n",
    "df_trends = pytrends.interest_over_time()\n",
    "print(\"Weekly trends columns:\", list(df_trends.columns))\n",
    "display(df_trends.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop isPartial if present, then resample to monthly average\n",
    "if \"isPartial\" in df_trends.columns:\n",
    "    df_trends = df_trends.drop(columns=[\"isPartial\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "df_monthly = df_trends.resample(\"MS\").mean().reset_index()\n",
    "df_monthly = df_monthly.rename(columns={\"date\": \"month\"})\n",
    "print(\"Monthly trends columns:\", list(df_monthly.columns))\n",
    "display(df_monthly.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "df_monthly.to_csv(DATA_DIR / \"google_trends_ai_music.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5) Deezer daily AI-upload points (press-reported)\n",
    "\n",
    "We store known daily upload counts as a simple time series and save them to `data/deezer_ai_daily_uploads.csv`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This lets us visualize platform-reported trends even without direct API access."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "deezer_points = [\n",
    "    {\"date\": \"2025-01-15\", \"daily_ai_uploads\": 10000},\n",
    "    {\"date\": \"2025-04-15\", \"daily_ai_uploads\": 20000},\n",
    "    {\"date\": \"2025-09-11\", \"daily_ai_uploads\": 30000},\n",
    "]\n",
    "df_deezer = pd.DataFrame(deezer_points)\n",
    "display(df_deezer)\n",
    "df_deezer.to_csv(DATA_DIR / \"deezer_ai_daily_uploads.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6) Visualize Google Trends (multi-series line chart)\n",
    "\n",
    "We use matplotlib for plotting:\n",
    "- `plt.figure(figsize=(w,h))` creates the canvas\n",
    "- `plt.plot(x, y)` draws lines\n",
    "- `plt.tight_layout()` reduces whitespace and prevents label cutoffs\n",
    "- `plt.savefig(path)` writes the chart to a PNG file\n",
    "- `plt.show()` displays the chart inline in the notebook"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_monthly = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / \"google_trends_ai_music.csv\")\n",
    "df_monthly[\"month\"] = pd.to_datetime(df_monthly[\"month\"])  # ensure datetime for x-axis\n",
    "df_monthly = df_monthly.sort_values(\"month\")\n",
    "\n",
    "query_cols = [c for c in df_monthly.columns if c != \"month\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "for c in query_cols:\n",
    "    plt.plot(df_monthly[\"month\"], df_monthly[c], label=c, linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Google Trends: Interest Over Time for AI-Music Queries\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Month\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Interest (0-100)\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / \"google_trends_ai_music.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7) Visualize Deezer points (annotated line chart)\n",
    "\n",
    "We annotate the points with their values so readers can see the exact numbers at a glance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_deezer = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / \"deezer_ai_daily_uploads.csv\")\n",
    "df_deezer[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df_deezer[\"date\"])  # convert strings to datetime\n",
    "df_deezer = df_deezer.sort_values(\"date\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "plt.plot(df_deezer[\"date\"], df_deezer[\"daily_ai_uploads\"], marker=\"o\", linestyle=\"-\", color=\"#ff7f0e\")\n",
    "for _, row in df_deezer.iterrows():\n",
    "    plt.annotate(f\"{row['daily_ai_uploads']}\", (row[\"date\"], row[\"daily_ai_uploads\"]),\n",
    "                 textcoords=\"offset points\", xytext=(0, 8), ha=\"center\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Deezer Daily Fully AI-Generated Track Uploads (Reported Points)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Daily uploads (count)\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / \"deezer_ai_daily_uploads.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8) Visualize SONICS aggregates (bar charts)\n",
    "\n",
    "We create simple bar charts from `fake_counts_by_source.csv` and `fake_counts_by_label.csv` if present."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "plotted = False\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left chart: counts by source (Suno/Udio)\n",
    "path_src = SONICS_DIR / \"fake_counts_by_source.csv\"\n",
    "if path_src.exists():\n",
    "    df_src = pd.read_csv(path_src)\n",
    "    axes[0].bar(df_src[\"source\"], df_src[\"count\"], color=\"#2ca02c\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_title(\"SONICS: Fake Songs by Source\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Source\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "    plotted = True\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    axes[0].text(0.5, 0.5, \"Missing counts_by_source\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\")\n",
    "    axes[0].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Right chart: counts by label (full/half/mostly fake)\n",
    "path_lbl = SONICS_DIR / \"fake_counts_by_label.csv\"\n",
    "if path_lbl.exists():\n",
    "    df_lbl = pd.read_csv(path_lbl)\n",
    "    axes[1].bar(df_lbl[\"label\"], df_lbl[\"count\"], color=\"#d62728\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_title(\"SONICS: Fake Songs by Label\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Label\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "    axes[1].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=20)\n",
    "    plotted = True\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    axes[1].text(0.5, 0.5, \"Missing counts_by_label\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\")\n",
    "    axes[1].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if plotted:\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / \"sonics_aggregates.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Optional: YouTube monthly counts\n",
    "\n",
    "The scripts support collecting a heuristic monthly count of AI-music-related YouTube uploads if you set `YOUTUBE_API_KEY`.\n",
    "This notebook skips that to keep everything no-API.\n",
    "\n",
    "Next steps:\n",
    "- Explore different queries in Google Trends\n",
    "- Join SONICS aggregates with Trends by month for comparative analysis\n",
    "- Add your own platform signals and visualize"
   ]
  }
 ]
}